# logs screen-control ------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Mock: the Logs screen. web-01.example.net runs Debian 13, less$
# installed. Lines hold what commands printed: colour, a title$
# and bell, a bidi override, bytes that are not UTF-8. They show$
# as ^[ and <U+202E> and <0xe9>; origin/main prints them raw to$
# the terminal (logging.go:146; file_logs_repository.go:96;$
# menu/logs_escape.golden).$
$
# Logs #########################################################$
$
# Log ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  File                 /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  Size                 264 bytes, 5 lines$
$
# All 5 lines --------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  2026/10/20 12:00:01 INFO: run 1: $ apt-get update$
   -  2026/10/20 12:00:02 INFO: run 1: | ^[[31mErr:1^[[0m$
      http://deb.example.net$
   -  2026/10/20 12:00:02 INFO: run 1: | ^[]0;a title^Gdone^[[2J$
   -  2026/10/20 12:00:03 INFO: run 2: | abc<U+202E>def$
   -  2026/10/20 12:00:03 INFO: run 2: | caf<0xe9>$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Open                 The whole log in less$
   2) Refresh              Read the log again$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-2 or q]:$
$
$

